   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoykiG",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "Regional New Zealand has so much potential to be more self-sufficient and to contribute to NZ. I'm standing because I believe all New Zealanders deserve equality in what it means to be an New Zealander, no matter where they live. Government should be there to serve the people and policy needs to enable people and business, not hold them back. Common-sense policy and a transparent, approachable style of government are important to me."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoykkR",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I was born and raised in Westport and have also owned a house in Richmond, Tasman, for 5 years. My farming career spans 30 years of dairy and beef farming. I entered local government and served as Mayor of Buller for 6 years. I led my district through major floods in 2021 and 2022 and the long-term recovery. I worked with different governments on regional development and investment strategy. I'm professional and effective in advocating for communities."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoykmc",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Improve household affordability.  Cutting the cost of electricity, groceries, banking, local rates"
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoykon",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Invest in Regions.  Returning mining royalties to community, tourism levies, infrastructure funding."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoykqy",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Cut Red Tape.  It must be made easier to do business, employ people and grow regional economies."
     }
    ],
