   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoylCk",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I am a class lefty, that is I do believe many workers, families, small business owners, disabled and family owned farms are getting a raw deal. I am running for the Alliance as the party is back for the same reasons were founded and that is to reverse the profound and damaging changes in the last 40 years. I believe in the ownership of public assets, universal healthcare, fairer taxation and universal public services."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoylEv",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "So really, to borrow the words from another Alliance candidate, \"I'm a political nobody\", but perhaps that is what voters are after; not another career politician but a person who has weathered the hard knocks of life and can therefore relate to those in the electorate. I am a fierce advocate and have been active in many community groups in Aotearoa and abroad."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoylH6",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Affordable housing. Establishing a Ministry of Works to help build public housing."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoylJH",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Access to healthcare. Funding community health hubs in each town with a Nurse Practitioner."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoylLS",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Buying back previously owned state assets - Electricity and to run as a service to bring down costs."
     }
    ],
